  "notes": "Psalm 25:6-12 with the Glória Patri, said while the priest washes his fingers. A document of its own for the same reason as ordinarium.iudica-me: it is a whole psalm portion, and the doxology attached to it falls away on its own days (Masses for the Dead and, in Masses of the season, from Passion Sunday to Holy Thursday) while the psalm stays. Witness do prints the doxology here by reference to its own shared block; the witness header declares the expansion. CIRCÚMDABO at w007 is accented on the antepenult because the a of dare is short — witness handmissal-eo accents the penult, adjudicated in the apparatus. ÁUDIAM at w012 is present subjunctive, not future indicative, which the form equally allows: it stands under ut with enárrem, whose subjunctive is unambiguous. BENEDÍCAM at w072 is the opposite case — future indicative, not subjunctive, standing in a main clause beside the futures Lavábo and circúmdabo. MANUS at w004 is accusative plural (the object of Lavábo) out of six readings the form allows, and DOMUS at w023 genitive singular out of five. MEI at w064 is the genitive of ego, which misereor governs, not the possessive meus — the same trap the corpus records for vestri at ordinarium.misereatur. MIRABÍLIA at w018 and INNOCÉNTES at w003 are adjectives standing as nouns; DIRÉCTO at w069 likewise, a neuter used as a noun after in.",
